From 66bcaa2bdcb0cf620fef72f836b70eb821eb6673 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Manjaya <chrismanjaya@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:16:43 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Replace visible error code with a code emoji
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Error replies now end with one emoji per error code on the same line
(400 🧪, 404 🕯️, 409 🧷, 503 🌩️, 500 🧠) instead of "Error code: 400".
The router logs "error reply sent" with sender and code for lookup.
Decorative emoji are removed from the error pools so the code emoji is
always the last one, and greetings like "halo" now count as Indonesian.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U4XsZULyGL5Ja6PMPZrTHh
